at mutual funds are regulated by the Securities and Exchange Commission. [00:21-00:40]\nDiverse Cartoon Investors: Ten diverse cartoon investors who invest in "WILL\'S FUND." [00:41-00:55]\nClosed-Ended Fund Investor: An investor representing a closed-ended fund, where shares are traded between investors rather than being redeemed from the fund itself. [01:34-01:45]\n\nSCENES:\nScene 1: Opening Title Screen: The video opens with the title "WHAT ARE MUTUAL FUNDS?" and the "WALL STREET SURVIVOR" logo. [00:00-00:20]\nScene 2: Will\'s Idea: An hourglass and a prize ribbon appear on Will, followed by question marks and a lightbulb, illustrating his idea to create a fund. [00:21-00:40]\nScene 3: "WILL\'S FUND" Established: Will stands alone as the fund is named and ten diverse cartoon investors appear opposite him. [00:41-00:55]\nScene 4: Net Asset Value (NAV) Introduced: The concept of NAV is introduced, showing a horizontal bar divided into three colored sections and a green pie chart building to show the pooled $10,000 total. [00:56-01:33]\nScene 5: Closed-Ended Funds: The video contrasts this with Closed-Ended Funds, showing a group of investors on the left and one investor on the right, illustrating that shares are traded between investors rather than being redeemed from the fund itself. [01:34-01:45]\n\nEVENTS:\nEvent 1: Mutual Fund Established: "WILL\'S FUND" is established with ten diverse cartoon investors investing $1,000 each, resulting in a pooled $10,000 total. [00:41-00:55]\nEvent 2: Fund Growth: The fund grows 10% to $11,000, with a $100 gain shown on a green pie chart. [00:56-01:33]\nYour question is this: Which of the following best describes the types of assets included within Will\'s "Assets Under Management" visual bar in the video, showcasing the composition of the mutual fund\'s holdings?'}]You are answering questions about a video using tools to retrieve information.

